        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Pyramids</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">21 July 1798</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near the village of Embabeh on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, in sight of the Pyramids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giza">Giza</a>, Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> (present-day Egypt)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The French army under General Bonaparte, in five divisions under Desaix, Reynier, Dugua, Vial and Bon; the Mamluk-led forces of Murad Bey, with elite armoured cavalry and fellahin militia, while Ibrahim Bey's army watched from across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The French took the fortified village of Embabeh and broke Murad Bey's army, which retreated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>. French losses were reported at about 300; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> and Ottoman casualties are estimated from several thousand to as many as 10,000.</span></div>
        </div>
